{title: Wonderful Peace}
{artist: Warren D. Cornell / William G. Cooper}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 55}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Three (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing, 1950), # 149)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Far away in the depths
[G]Of my [C]spirit to[G]night
[G]Rolls a melody [A7]sweeter than [D]psalm;
[D]In ce[G]lestial-like strains
[G]It un[C]ceasingly falls
[C]O’er my [D7]soul like an infinite [G]calm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Peace, peace, [C]wonderful [G]peace,
[G]Coming [Em]down from the [A7]Father a[D]bove!
[D]Sweep [G]over my spirit for[C]ever, I pray
[C]In [D7]fathomless billows of [G]love!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]What a treasure I have
[G]In this [C]wonderful [G]peace,
[G]Buried deep in the [A7]heart of my [D]soul,
[D]So se[G]cure that no power
[G]Can [C]mine it away,
[C]While the [D7]years of eternity [G]roll!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I am resting tonight
[G]In this [C]wonderful [G]peace,
[G]Resting sweetly in [A7]Jesus’ con[D]trol;
[D]For I’m [G]kept from all danger
[G]By [C]night and by day,
[C]And His [D7]glory is flooding my [G]soul!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]And I think when I rise
[G]To that [C]city of [G]peace,
[G]Where the anchor of [A7]peace I shall [D]see,
[D]That one [G]strain of the song
[G]Which the [C]ransomed will sing
[C]In that [D7]heavenly kingdom will [G]be:
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Ah, soul! are you here
[G]Without [C]comfort and [G]rest,
[G]Marching down the rough [A7]pathway of [D]time?
[D]Make [G]Jesus your friend
[G]Ere the [C]shadows grow dark;
[C]O ac[D7]cept this sweet peace so sub[G]lime!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
